message: "If you use this simulated proof-of-concept software or dataset in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "hvdc-graded-dielectric-sim-poc: Coupled Electro-Thermal and Bipolar Charge-Transport Simulated POC for Radially Graded HVDC Polymeric Insulation"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-26"
authors:
  - family-names: "Singh"
    given-names: "Abhishek"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-6913-096X"
  - name: "Google Gemini"
    alias: "AI Research Collaborator"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Abhishek1033ubuntu/hvdc-graded-dielectric-sim-poc"
url: "https://github.com/Abhishek1033ubuntu/hvdc-graded-dielectric-sim-poc"
abstract: >-
  Simulated Proof-of-Concept (in silico) modeling coupled 1D cylindrical heat conduction,
  Poisson electrostatics, and CFL-stabilized bipolar charge transport in 525 kV HVDC
  extruded solid polymeric cable insulation under heavy conductor thermal gradients and
  Voltage Polarity Reversal (VPR). Evaluates standard XLPE against a radially graded
  Perfluorocyclobutyl (PFCB) / Oligosiloxane / Fluorinated Polyimide (6FDA-TFMB) block
  terpolymer reinforced with surface-silanized isotopically enriched 11B15N nanosheets
  (underlying Mode B material to be developed / not yet POC'd experimentally).
